# API Controllers

## Controller pattern

```csharp
[ApiController]
[Authorize]
[Route("api/v1/examples")]
public sealed class ExamplesController : ControllerBase;
```

Use permission policies on each operation or controller as appropriate.

```csharp
[Authorize(Policy = AppPermissions.UsersManage)]
public class UsersController(...) { }

[Authorize(Policy = ProductPermissions.RecordsRead)]
public sealed class RecordsController(...) { }
```

## Routes

All application routes are explicit and start with `api/v1`. Health and development OpenAPI endpoints are operational exceptions.

## Platform controllers

- `AuthController` — CSRF, login, logout, current user, profile, password
- `UsersController` — admin-created users and temporary passwords
- `RolesController` — global role and permission management
- `AuditController` — security audit read API

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — new controller without [Authorize]
[ApiController]
public class ExampleController : ControllerBase { ... }

// ✅ GOOD — explicit policy
[Authorize(Policy = ProductPermissions.ExamplesRead)]
public sealed class ExampleController : ControllerBase;
```
